  "worked_solution": "Let's simplify one of the given integrals:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{7}^{2}(-5)\\,f(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =15 \\\\ (-5){\\int }_{7}^{2}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =15 \\\\ 5{\\int }_{2}^{7}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =15 \\\\ {\\int }_{2}^{7}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, from the adjacent intervals rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-1}^{7}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{-1}^{2}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{2}^{7}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =1+3 \\\\  & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
